        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Ab tumhare sawal ka jawab: Moderate inflation (2-3% per year) actually healthy hai economy ke liye! Isse producers ko motivation milti hai production badhane ki. Lekin HIGH inflation (7-8%+) harmful hai — common man ki purchasing power ghat jaati hai. Zero inflation bhi achha nahi, isse deflation ka risk hota hai."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Hain?? Deflation matlab kya Sir?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Deflation matlab prices ka continuously GIREGA! Sunne mein achha lagta hai na? Lekin bahut dangerous hai — logon ko lagta hai prices aur gir jayenge, to wo buying postpone kar dete hain. Isse demand ghat jaati hai, businesses close hote hain. Japan ne 1990s mein ye dekha tha. Isliye RBI target karti hai 4% (+/- 2%) ka moderate inflation."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab thoda inflation good, zyada bad, zero bhi bad! Balance chahiye!"
        }
      ],
