        "total": 65
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "DEMAND-PULL INFLATION: Jab economy mein bahut paisa aa jaata hai (government spending badha, loans saste ho gaye, ya logon ki income badhi), to demand badh jaati hai. Lekin supply utni jaldi nahi badh paati. Isse prices upar jaate hain. Classical economics mein kehte hain: 'Too much money chasing too few goods.'"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab jaise COVID ke baad lockdown khula, to sabne shopping karna start kiya, demand badhi?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Exactly! Post-lockdown pent-up demand ne prices badha diye many sectors mein. Ek aur example: Jab government employees ko 7th Pay Commission ke baad salary increase mili, to unki purchasing power badhi, demand badhi, kuch categories mein inflation aaya. Ye Demand-Pull ka real-life case hai."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Achhaaaa... to achhi baat (salary increase) se bhi inflation ho sakta hai!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
