      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "COST-PUSH INFLATION: Jab production cost badh jaata hai (raw materials expensive ho gaye, wages badh gaye, ya taxes badh gaye), to producers apni costs recover karne ke liye prices badha dete hain. Supply side ki problem hai ye. Example: Crude oil prices international market mein badhe, to India mein petrol-diesel mehanga hua, isse transport costs badhe, ultimately sab products mehange ho gaye."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir ye to chain reaction jaisa hai! Ek cheez ki cost badhi to baaki sab bhi badh gaye!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Perfect understanding! Isse hi 'ripple effect' kehte hain. ⭐ BPSC TRE Favorite: Bihar mein jab monsoon weak hota hai, crops ki yield kam hoti hai, food prices badh jaate hain — ye bhi cost-push inflation ka example hai. Natural calamities, supply chain disruptions — ye sab cost-push causes hain."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab demand-pull mein demand zyada, cost-push mein supply side problem!"
        }
      },
