      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "CPI (Consumer Price Index): Ye measure karta hai ek typical household ka cost of living kitna badh raha hai. Isme food, housing, clothing, transport, healthcare, education — sab ka weighted average price change dekha jaata hai. Base year = 2012. Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation (MOSPI) isse calculate karti hai monthly."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir 'weighted average' matlab kya? Sabka equal importance nahi hai kya?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Bilkul nahi! Food aur beverages ka weight CPI mein sabse zyada hai (~46%), kyunki average Indian household ka sabse bada expense yahi hai. Housing ka ~10%, clothing ~6% weight hai. Different items ka different weightage hota hai importance ke hisaab se. Ye weightage household consumption survey se milta hai."
