    {
      "card_id": "card_25_tax_structure_intro",
      "card_slug": "card_25_tax_structure_intro",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "tax_intro",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 25,
        "total": 65
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Ab inflation se tax structure ki taraf! Dekho, government ko paisa chahiye public services provide karne ke liye — roads, schools, hospitals. Ye paisa aata hai mainly TAXES se. Tax structure matlab — kis-kis tarah ke taxes hain, kaun kitna pay karta hai, aur kitna efficient/fair hai system."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir tax to bas Income Tax aur GST hain na? Baaki kya-kya hai?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Nahi nahi! Bohot saare types hain. Pehle ek fundamental classification samjho: DIRECT TAX aur INDIRECT TAX. Direct Tax = jo person jis par laga hai wo khud hi pay karta hai (Income Tax, Property Tax). Indirect Tax = jo ek person par laga hai lekin burden dusre par shift ho jaata hai (GST, Excise Duty)."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Hain?? Burden shift kaise ho jaata hai?"
