    {
      "card_id": "card_27_indirect_tax_detail",
      "card_slug": "card_27_indirect_tax_detail",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "indirect_tax_detail",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 27,
        "total": 65
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "INDIRECT TAX: Ye goods aur services par lagta hai. Seller tax government ko deta hai, lekin actual burden consumer (final buyer) par hota hai through higher prices. Examples: GST, Customs Duty (import/export par), Excise Duty (manufacturing par — ab GST mein merge). Ye regressive nature ke hote hain — rich-poor sabke liye same rate."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir example dijiye burden shift ka!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Dekho: Tum chocolate kharido ₹20 ki. Usme 18% GST included hai matlab ₹3 tax. Shopkeeper wo ₹3 government ko dega, lekin actually tumne pay kiya! Shopkeeper ne price mein include kar diya. Burden shift ho gaya tumhare upar. Isliye indirect tax regressive hai — ameer-gareeb dono same ₹3 tax pay karenge chocolate par."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Ohhh! Matlab direct tax mein main khud pay karta hoon, indirect mein koi aur collect karke deta hai!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
