    {
      "card_id": "card_33_progressive_regressive_intro",
      "card_slug": "card_33_progressive_regressive_intro",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "progressive_regressive_intro",
      "level": 5,
      "progress": {
        "current": 33,
        "total": 65
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Ab samajhte hain tax systems ki fairness/equity ka angle. Taxes teen types ke hote hain nature ke hisaab se: 1) PROGRESSIVE (ameer par zyada burden), 2) REGRESSIVE (gareeb par relatively zyada burden), 3) PROPORTIONAL (sabke liye same percentage). Ye classification UPSC/BPSC ka favorite hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir pehle aapne bola tha Income Tax progressive hai. Matlab?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Haan! Progressive Tax mein tax RATE income ke saath badhta hai. Example: ₹2.5 lakh tak nil tax, ₹5 lakh tak 5%, ₹10 lakh tak 20%, ₹10 lakh+ par 30%. Jaise income badhti hai, rate bhi badhta hai. Ye equity ensure karta hai — ability to pay principle. Rich log apni capacity ke hisaab se zyada contribute karte hain."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Achhaaaa! To progressive matlab rate income ke saath increase hota hai!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_34_regressive_tax",
        "button_text": "Regressive Tax ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_34_regressive_tax",
      "card_slug": "card_34_regressive_tax",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "regressive_tax",
      "level": 5,
      "progress": {
        "current": 34,
        "total": 65
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "REGRESSIVE TAX: Jisme gareeb logo par relatively ZYADA burden padta hai unke income ke proportion mein. Indirect taxes (GST, Excise) generally regressive hote hain. Example: Chocolate par ₹3 GST — ameer aadmi ke liye negligible, lekin daily wage worker ke liye significant. Same absolute amount, but different relative impact."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab ameer-gareeb dono ₹3 pay kar rahe hain, lekin gareeb ke liye ₹3 ka value zyada hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Exactly! Isliye indirect taxes ko regressive kehte hain — ye income level ko consider nahi karte. ₹1 crore income wala bhi same GST, ₹10,000 income wala bhi. Proportionally gareeb par zyada burden. BPSC mein yahi equity/inequality ka angle puchha jaata hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir to proportional tax kya hota hai?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_35_proportional_tax",
        "button_text": "Proportional Tax ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_35_proportional_tax",
      "card_slug": "card_35_proportional_tax",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "proportional_tax",
      "level": 5,
      "progress": {
        "current": 35,
        "total": 65
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "PROPORTIONAL TAX (Flat Tax): Jisme sabke liye SAME RATE hota hai income ke percentage ke roop mein, chahe income kitni bhi ho. Example: Agar flat 10% tax hai — ₹1 lakh income par ₹10,000 tax, ₹10 lakh par ₹1 lakh tax. Rate same (10%), absolute amount alag. Currently India mein pure proportional tax system nahi hai income tax mein."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir to teen types: Progressive = rate badhta, Regressive = gareeb par zyada burden, Proportional = same rate sabke liye!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Perfect summary! Ab ek BPSC trap batata hoon: Corporate Tax (30% flat) proportional lag sakta hai, lekin actually progressive nature ka hai kyunki only profit-making entities pay karte hain. Small businesses exemptions milte hain. Ye nuance UPSC/BPSC mein test hota hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Ye to tricky hai! Classification simple nahi hai hamesha!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_36_tax_equity_efficiency",
        "button_text": "Equity vs Efficiency ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_36_tax_equity_efficiency",
      "card_slug": "card_36_tax_equity_efficiency",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "tax_equity_efficiency",
      "level": 5,
      "progress": {
        "current": 36,
        "total": 65
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Tax system design mein do competing objectives hain: EQUITY (fairness — sabke saath nyay) aur EFFICIENCY (economic growth disturb na ho). Progressive taxes zyada equitable hain but complexity badhti hai. Indirect taxes efficient hain (collect karna easy) but regressive hain. Ideal system dono balance karta hai."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir matlab koi perfect tax system nahi hai? Trade-off hamesha rahega?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Bilkul sahi! Har system mein pros-cons hain. India mixed approach use karta hai — Direct taxes (progressive, equitable) + Indirect taxes (efficient, broad-based). GST ne efficiency improve ki, lekin equity concerns abhi bhi hain. ⭐ BPSC TRE mein frequently policy analysis questions mein ye angle aata hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Samajh gaya Sir! Mixed system best compromise hai!"
        }
